From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AudioPulse: open the capture stream on the input device

AudioPulse's constructor hands outputDevice to AudioInputPulse, so the
capture stream is connected to whatever was chosen as the playback
device. With the default device on both sides nobody notices. A client
that names its devices through SetCurrentAudioInput() and
SetCurrentAudioOutput() before Start() gets a capture stream on the
playback sink's name; PulseAudio has no source by that name, the record
stream fails, the input reports itself uninitialised, and
AudioIO::Create() drops the whole PulseAudio backend for ALSA, which
opens neither device by those names and falls back to "default" for
both.

tdlib-purple on LuneOS names the PulseAudio call sink and source,
voipcall and webcall, so its calls fell back to ALSA's default device
instead of the call devices audiod routes.

Pass inputDevice to AudioInputPulse. -Wextra pointed at it all along:

  AudioPulse.cpp:128:36: warning: unused parameter 'inputDevice'

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp b/os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp
index 701d851..f02ece8 100644
--- a/os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp
+++ b/os/linux/AudioPulse.cpp
@@ -193,7 +193,7 @@ AudioPulse::AudioPulse(std::string inputDevice, std::string outputDevice){
 	isLocked=false;
 
 	output=new AudioOutputPulse(context, mainloop, outputDevice);
-	input=new AudioInputPulse(context, mainloop, outputDevice);
+	input=new AudioInputPulse(context, mainloop, inputDevice);
 }
 
 AudioPulse::~AudioPulse(){
